{
  "synthetic_id": "synthetic_twin_24623966_01",
  "source_doc_id": "24623966",
  "title": "NADPH oxidase 4 and VEGF receptor 2 in retinopathy of prematurity",
  "abstract": "NADPH oxidase 4 mediates vascular endothelial growth factor receptor 2-induced intravitreal neovascularization in a rat model of retinopathy of prematurity. NADPH oxidase-generated reactive oxygen species are involved in angiogenesis. NOX4 is the most prevalent isoform of NADPH oxidase in vascular endothelial cells. In oxygen-induced retinopathy, NOX4 expression decreases during development and increases at postnatal day 18. Retinal cryosections show increased colabeling of NOX4 with lectin-stained endothelial cells in OIR compared to room air. VEGF induces ROS generation and activates VEGFR2 and STAT3 in endothelial cells. Knockdown of NOX4 reduces VEGF-induced ROS and inhibits VEGFR2 activation, but does not abolish it. NOX4 deficiency also prevents STAT3 activation in response to VEGF. VEGF-stimulated endothelial cell proliferation is inhibited by NOX4 or STAT3 knockdown. These findings suggest that NOX4 regulates VEGFR2-mediated neovascularization through STAT3 activation in retinopathy of prematurity."
} 

{
  "synthetic_id": "synthetic_twin_24623966_02",
  "source_doc_id": "24623966",
  "title": "Role of NADPH oxidase 4 and reactive oxygen species in retinal angiogenesis",
  "abstract": "NADPH oxidase 4 is critical for vascular endothelial growth factor receptor 2-induced intravitreal neovascularization in retinopathy of prematurity. NADPH oxidase-generated reactive oxygen species contribute to angiogenesis. NOX4 is the primary NADPH oxidase isoform in vascular endothelial cells. In oxygen-induced retinopathy, NOX4 expression decreases during development but increases at postnatal day 18. Retinal cryosections show increased colabeling of NOX4 with lectin-stained endothelial cells in OIR compared to room air. VEGF induces ROS generation and activates VEGFR2 and STAT3 in endothelial cells. Knockdown of NOX4 reduces VEGF-induced ROS and inhibits VEGFR2 activation. NOX4 deficiency also prevents STAT3 activation in response to VEGF. VEGF-stimulated endothelial cell proliferation is inhibited by NOX4 or STAT3 knockdown. These results indicate that NOX4 regulates VEGFR2-mediated neovascularization through STAT3 activation in retinopathy of prematurity."
} 

