  "title": "Novel Mutations in CHST6 Gene Associated with Macular Corneal Dystrophy",
  "abstract": "A family with Macular corneal dystrophy (MCD) was studied to identify mutations in the CHST6 gene. The patients showed abnormal deposition of keratan sulfate (KS) in the corneal stroma, as revealed by colloidal iron staining. Genomic DNA from 11 family members was analyzed, and compound heterozygous mutations c.892C > T and c.1072T > C were detected in three affected individuals. These mutations resulted in the substitution of a stop codon for glutamine at codon 298 (p.Q298X) and a missense change at codon 358, tyrosine to histidine (p.Y358H). The mutations were not found in 100 control subjects, suggesting a novel genetic basis for MCD. Iron and keratan sulfate were found to be present in the corneal stroma, with no direct biochemical interaction between them. Collagen fibers were observed to be abnormally thickened, and the mutations were linked to impaired KS metabolism. The study highlights the role of CHST6 in maintaining normal corneal structure and function."
